Z||000000||curtis||09-02-2001||09:08 PM||||My 88 formula died about two moths ago. It rotates, but will not start. We have changed all the injectors, pump regulator, ignition module, coil, and the timing chain and made sure it was timed correctly about three times||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||09-02-2001||09:20 PM||||Did you change the pick-up coil in the distributor? What are you not getting? Is there spark when you crank it or not? If you push the shreader valve on the fuel rail does air or fuel come out?<BR>If no spark possible the pick-up coil is bad. (common problem with V-6's)<BR>The procedure to replace it is:<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-pickupcoil.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-pickupcoil.html</A> <P>If you have spark but no fuel, is the fuel pump working? Fuel filter clogged? <BR>We need more info in order to aid in other things to look at.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||curtis||09-02-2001||10:08 PM||||Yes we are getting 48 pounds of fuel pressure. And we are getting fuel.  and we are getting spark in the 5 and 3.  And we have replaced the fuel filter. ||||reg||1
